  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(\\land)$ and \"or\" $(\\lor)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A \\land B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A \\lor B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $A$ is true, and $B$ is true. Therefore, the result is true:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n\\underbrace{5 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is odd} }_A \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{or}}_{\\lor} \\quad \n\\underbrace{-5 \\in \\mathbb{Z}}_B\n&\\:\\:\\equiv\\: \\text{true} \\lor \\textrm{true} \\equiv \\textrm{true}\n\\end{align*}",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
