  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-175666\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(\\land)$ and \"or\" $(\\lor)$ logical connectives:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>The statement $A \\land B$ is true if <em>both</em> $A$ and $B$ are true.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>The statement $A \\lor B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or <em>both</em> $A$ and $B$ are true.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>In our case, $A$ is true, and $B$ is true. Therefore, the result is true:</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n\\underbrace{5 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is odd} }_A \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{or}}_{\\lor} \\quad \n\\underbrace{-5 \\in \\mathbb{Z}}_B\n&amp;\\:\\:\\equiv\\: \\text{true} \\lor \\textrm{true} \\equiv \\textrm{true}\n\\end{align*}</p>\n</div>",
